{"schema":"statespace/lesson@1","id":"S5.L4","tier":"bridge","title":"The holds lifecycle","draft":true,"kcs":["KC-5.holds-lifecycle"],"objective":"Write a hold's lifecycle in TLA+ with a counter for resolutions, state that a hold never resolves twice as an invariant, and give a behavior for each outcome and a step the spec forbids.","segments":[{"id":"s1","title":"One hold","minutes":14,"kcs":["KC-5.holds-lifecycle"],"blocks":[{"type":"item","role":"prequestion","family":"GEN-trace-allowed","template":"t1","kcs":["KC-5.holds-lifecycle"],"choice":{"prompt":"Which formula says \"a hold never resolves twice\"?","options":[{"id":"A","text":"`<>(res >= 1)`, read as a property of the whole behavior","why":"That says a hold eventually resolves, which is a different kind of property.","mis":"dp:C5"},{"id":"B","text":"`~(hst = \"captured\" /\\ hst = \"released\")`, read as an invariant","why":"It is true of every state, because one state holds one value. It cannot remember two events.","mis":"dp:T11"},{"id":"C","text":"`res <= 1` as an invariant (`res` counts resolutions)","why":"A history variable makes past events visible to a predicate on the current state."}],"key":"C"},"itemRev":"28e0cb87992ebfc0"},{"type":"prose","md":"A hold reserves funds for a payment. `Place` takes it from available to held. From held it is either captured, and the money moves, or released, and the funds go back. In the spec these are three system actions on one hold, and the property to state is that it never resolves twice.\n\nA state cannot say that. It holds one value for `hst` and remembers nothing about how it got there. So add a history variable, `res`, that counts resolutions: every `Capture` and every `Release` adds 1. Then the sentence is an ordinary invariant, `res <= 1`.\n\nA second kind of statement is about a step, not a state. `StaysResolved` says that from a captured or released hold the next state is the same. It is an action property, so TLC checks it on the Bench, and the tab checks invariants. The implication is in parentheses because TLA+'s own parser rejects the bare form, although Spectacle's accepts it {{run:RUN-spectacle-s5s8}}."},{"type":"instrument","ins":"INS-spectacle","cell":1,"callOnFirstRun":true,"recorded":"RUN-tlc-lifecycle","direction":"Model asserts: `TypeOK` and `NeverTwice` hold in every reachable state. A resolved hold has nothing left to do, so this model turns the deadlock check off.","code":{"lang":"tla","text":"---- MODULE HoldsLifecycle ----\nEXTENDS Naturals\nVARIABLES hst, res\nvars == <<hst, res>>\n\nTypeOK == /\\ hst \\in {\"available\", \"held\", \"captured\", \"released\"}\n          /\\ res \\in 0..2\n\nInit == hst = \"available\" /\\ res = 0\n\nPlace   == hst = \"available\" /\\ hst' = \"held\"     /\\ UNCHANGED res\nCapture == hst = \"held\"      /\\ hst' = \"captured\" /\\ res' = res + 1\nRelease == hst = \"held\"      /\\ hst' = \"released\" /\\ res' = res + 1\n\nNext == Place \\/ Capture \\/ Release\nSpec == Init /\\ [][Next]_vars\n\nNeverTwice == res <= 1\n\\* An action property: a resolved hold stays resolved. TLC checks it on the Bench.\nStaysResolved == [][(hst \\in {\"captured\", \"released\"}) => hst' = hst]_hst\n====\n\\* INIT Init, NEXT Next, INVARIANT TypeOK, INVARIANT NeverTwice, deadlock check off","editable":true},"call":{"prompt":"Can `res` reach 2 in this lifecycle?","options":[{"id":"A","text":"No.","why":"Each resolution needs `hst = \"held\"` and leaves it, so after one of them neither action is enabled."},{"id":"B","text":"Yes: `Capture` and `Release` are both enabled in held, so both fire.","why":"One step takes one action. Two enabled actions are two choices, never two events.","mis":"dp:T16"},{"id":"C","text":"It depends on the scheduler.","why":"The model covers every schedule, so one answer holds for all of them.","mis":"dp:C4"}],"key":"A","keyRun":"RUN-tlc-lifecycle","surprise":"no"},"after":"No schedule reaches 2. With the deadlock check off, TLC finishes the exploration with no error {{run:RUN-tlc-lifecycle}}. A hold that has resolved enables nothing, which TLC's default flags would report as a deadlock, as in the last lesson.","itemRev":"1ebc1175892d5937"},{"type":"item","role":"segment","family":"GEN-trace-allowed","template":"t1","kcs":["KC-5.holds-lifecycle"],"choice":{"prompt":"A variant lets `Release` fire from `captured` as well as from `held`. Which prefix is the first to break `res <= 1`?","options":[{"id":"A","text":"`Place`, `Release`","why":"One resolution, so `res` is 1, which the invariant allows.","mis":"dp:T11"},{"id":"B","text":"`Place`, `Capture`, `Release`","why":"The second resolution takes `res` to 2."},{"id":"C","text":"`Place`, `Capture`, then a step that changes nothing","why":"A step that changes nothing is not a resolution, so `res` stays 1.","mis":"dp:T7"}],"key":"B"},"itemRev":"1141dca6d6da7ee7"}]},{"id":"s2","title":"Exit","minutes":4,"kcs":["KC-5.holds-lifecycle"],"blocks":[{"type":"item","role":"exit","family":"GEN-trace-allowed","template":"t2","kcs":["KC-5.holds-lifecycle"],"choice":{"prompt":"In the lifecycle's state `hst = \"captured\"`, `res = 1`, which actions are enabled?","options":[{"id":"A","text":"`Release`: it gives the money back to the payer.","why":"`Release` needs `hst = \"held\"`. The spec has no action that undoes a capture.","mis":"dp:T10"},{"id":"B","text":"None: the behavior ends once the hold has resolved.","why":"Behaviors are infinite. When nothing is enabled, the hold stutters forever.","mis":"dp:T8"},{"id":"C","text":"None: the behavior stays here and stutters forever.","why":"`Place` needs available and the other two need held. Only stuttering remains."}],"key":"C"},"itemRev":"bbc005ecf112d10e"},{"type":"card","variant":"twin","title":"TigerBeetle","md":"TigerBeetle's two-phase transfers have the same shape. \"A pending transfer can only be posted or voided once,\" and a repeat returns `pending_transfer_already_posted`, `pending_transfer_already_voided` or `pending_transfer_expired` (sections \"Resolve Funds\" and \"Errors\", read 2026-10-23; see [docs.tigerbeetle.com](https://docs.tigerbeetle.com/coding/two-phase-transfers/)). Which disabled branch of your spec matches each error? Pins: {{run:RUN-twin-pins}}.","runs":["RUN-twin-pins"]},{"type":"card","variant":"reading","title":"Reading","md":"Learn TLA+ by Hillel Wayne, read 2026-10-23. Core › Writing an Invariant (`core/invariants.html`). Topics › Auxiliary Variables, section \"History Variables\" (`topics/aux-vars.html#history-variables`). Core › Action Properties (`core/action-properties.html`). All are at [learntla.com](https://learntla.com/)."},{"type":"card","variant":"build-this","title":"Build this","md":"Next, write your own holds lifecycle with the resolution counter and check that a hold never resolves twice.","lab":"LAB-5.3","minutes":25}]}],"minutes":18,"rail":[{"id":"s1","title":"One hold"},{"id":"s2","title":"Exit"}],"establishes":{"claims":[],"specimens":[]},"runs":{"RUN-spectacle-s5s8":{"id":"RUN-spectacle-s5s8","title":"Spectacle at 5827c22 on the Stage 5 and Stage 8 specs: operator coverage, local EXTENDS, speed and the state-pair check, against TLC 1.8.0 (W0-S04)","engine":"spectacle","version":"5827c22043216ea422b9dada64fdec19d6d8e5c4","binary_sha256":"5c9868419e8756ba5e96d578a979e1a4e12da1cc910568881ec790c02918b0ff","image":"mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.63.0-noble@sha256:eff16c30e6f3f4af0a03fa4b706120d5e9b0891c344a27d64559aff5900a4a27","argv":[["node","scripts/spikes/W0-S04/fetch-spectacle.mjs"],["node","scripts/spikes/W0-S04/tlc.mjs"],["node","scripts/spikes/W0-S04/node-run.mjs"],["docker","run","--rm","--memory=6g","--shm-size=2g","--name","w0s04-pw","-e","HOST_UID=<uid>","-e","HOST_GID=<gid>","-v","<repo>:/repo","-v","<cache>:/cache","mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.63.0-noble","node","/repo/scripts/spikes/W0-S04/browsers.mjs"],["node","scripts/spikes/W0-S04/record.mjs"]],"inputs":[{"path":"scripts/spikes/W0-S04/specs/probes/ProbeActionParse.cfg","sha256":"e904d3